-- Design Warning Section

attribute DESIGN_WARNING of XCVC1902_VSVD1760 : entity is
   "The Versal ACAP device contains two TAPs in series: " &
        "the Arm DAP and the main device TAP. See the " &
        "JTAG and Boundary-Scan section in the Xilinx Versal ACAP " &
        "Technical Reference Manual (AM011) at https://www.xilinx.com " &
        "for details. To correctly model the JTAG chain of devices, " &
        "each Versal ACAP device instance in the JTAG chain from a " &
        "schematic netlist should be represented by the following " &
        "in the corresponding JTAG chain model a JTAG/boundary-scan test tool: " &
        "1. Arm DAP, represented by the versal_arm_dap.bsd file; " &
        "2. Versal ACAP, represented by a Versal ACAP BSDL file such as this BSDL file. " &
        "NOTE: If the Versal ACAP is secured with settings that disable JTAG " &
        "access to the Arm DAP, replace the versal_arm_dap.bsd (above) " &
        "with the versal_dummy_dap.bsd. " &
    "Certain Versal devices can be affected by a 3-state output issue. " &
       "See https://support.xilinx.com/s/article/76889 for affected devices and details. " &
       "This issue affects the following JTAG functions and conditions: " &
       "1. JTAG TDO errors might occur on leading 1-value least-significant output bits " &
           "when the TDO (VCCO_503 power pin) operates at 3.3V or 2.5V and " &
           "when JTAG tools do not include a work-around. " &
           "See https://support.xilinx.com/s/article/76893 for details and work-arounds. " &
       "2. The JTAG EXTEST vectors might fail at MIO or HDIO pins when these pins " &
           "are operated at 3.3V or 2.5V and when JTAG tools do not avoid or work-around " &
           "the issue conditions. See https://support.xilinx.com/s/article/76894 " &
           "for details and work-arounds. " &
       "For JTAG tools that do not avoid, or do not include work-arounds, or that are " &
       "unknown to avoid/work-around for the two listed issues, a special variant of " &
       "the BSDL files for affected device-packages is provided in the " &
       "AR76889_workaround subdirectory of the Versal BSDL download .zip " &
       "archive available from the Device Models area at " &
       "https://www.xilinx.com/support/download.html " &
    "This BSDL file is a device model of a fully-powered and UNCONFIGURED device. " &
        "The functions described in this BSDL file are available when all of the " &
        "conditions listed in the BSDL file header comments are met, including: " &
        "device fully-powered; device is unconfigured; free-running clock to REF_CLK; " &
        "POR_B pin is High. " &
        "Otherwise, if the listed conditions are not met, then one or more functions " &
        "described in this BSDL file might not be available or the IDCODE " &
        "reported by the device might be invalid. " &
        "Recommended: Keep the device unconfigured during boundary-scan to " &
        "ensure device JTAG behavior matches this BSDL device model by setting " &
        "the inputs to the device MODE[3:0] pins to 0000 (the JTAG boot mode " &
        "setting) before power-on (or at least before and through the Low-to-High " &
        "transition of the input to the POR_B pin. " &
    "All IOBs prior to configuration, and unused and output-only IOBs following " &
        "configuration, will sense their pad values during boundary-scan with an " &
        "LVCMOS-type input buffer. An input voltage level that does not meet the " &
        "LVCMOS input-High or input-Low requirement might not be captured as " &
        "'1' or '0', respectively. For post-configuration boundary-scan only: " &
        "If an IOB is configured to use an input standard that uses VREF pins, " &
        "then the boundary-scan test vectors must keep the used VREF pins 3-stated.";

end XCVC1902_VSVD1760;

